    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "RBI was nationalized in 1949, whereas SEBI attained statutory body status in 1992.",
        "IRDAI is one of the few financial regulators headquartered in Hyderabad, making it a frequent topic in general awareness questions.",
        "Remember the respective governing acts: RBI Act 1934, SEBI Act 1992, and IRDA Act 1999."
      ],
      "id": "ncs6xr9"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "RBI acts as the central bank regulating monetary policy, commercial banks, and currency issuance under the RBI Act, 1934.",
        "SEBI oversees the securities market and stock exchanges to protect retail investors under the SEBI Act, 1992.",
        "IRDAI regulates and promotes the insurance and re-insurance sector under the IRDA Act, 1999.",
        "RBI and SEBI operate from Mumbai, whereas IRDAI is headquartered in Hyderabad."
